            listing, including budget walking pads, so a machine qualified only if its manufacturer
            names a specific cushioning system and says something about how it works. The second
            was the frame: cushioning only works as designed when the frame under it is stiff, so we
            limited the list to full-size machines with 60-inch decks from established brands. The
            third was agreement: every figure on a spec line matches across the manufacturer and at
            least one other source.
          </p>
          <p>
            We did not rank by impact-reduction percentages. Several brands publish them, but each
            measures against its own baseline using its own method, so they cannot be compared. We
            also left out machines whose current specifications we could not pin down: Sole is known
            for its Cushion Flex Whisper Deck, but its 2026 F-series pages describe a revised deck and
