        <div class="mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">Common Mistakes Buying a Cushioned Treadmill</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Most of these come from treating cushioning as a number to maximise rather than one part of a comfortable machine.</p>
          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying the softest deck</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">A deck that sinks under you feels plush for minutes and tiring for an hour. Look for moderate give and a quick return, and read how independent reviews describe the feel.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Comparing impact percentages</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Each brand measures its own figure its own way. A higher percentage on one listing does not mean a softer or better deck than a lower one on another.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Ignoring the warranty on the cushioning</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Elastomers and shock absorbers wear. A lifetime or long warranty on the deck’s cushioning parts is a better signal of quality than any marketing name.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Expecting the deck to do the work of the settings</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Incline walking, gradual build-up and good shoes reduce load more than any deck. Buy a well-cushioned machine, then use it in a low-impact way.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

